# Git LFS — large committed native binaries.
#
# The Swift xcframework static libraries are CI-assembled, committed
# artifacts (assembled on macos-15 by .github/workflows/xcframework.yml when
# the uniffi FFI surface changes; refreshed via
# tooling/connect/apply-xcframework-artifact.sh), tracked via LFS so the
# repository does not accumulate ~120 MB of staticlib churn on every
# refresh. SPM consumers resolve the xcframework from git; git-lfs is bundled
# with Xcode (CLI `swift build` users run `git lfs install` once).
#
# Other Path B natives (Go `native/`, Kotlin `native/`, Python `spoke_connect/`)
# stay as plain git blobs: Go modules resolve through the module proxy (no LFS
# smudge), and the Kotlin/Python dylibs are small build inputs for the
# Maven/PyPI artifacts.
#
# The C carrier's dynamic libraries (staged by tooling/connect/cpp-build.mjs,
# Windows refresh via the `windows-smoke` lane of
# .github/workflows/cpp-connect.yml) are ~6 MB each and are tracked the same
# way. Its import library (`*.dll.lib`, ~150 KB) and `provenance.json` stay
# plain git blobs: they are small, and every checkout — including the lanes
# that only hash or diff the record — has to read them without an LFS fetch.
# C/C++ consumers clone the repo, so they need git-lfs (`git lfs install`
# once, `git lfs pull` in an existing clone).
crates/spoke-connect/bindings/swift/xcframework/**/*.a filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
crates/spoke-connect/bindings/cpp/native/**/*.dll filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
crates/spoke-connect/bindings/cpp/native/**/*.dylib filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# The C and C++ contract header bytes are part of the published carrier record:
# `tooling/connect/cpp-build.mjs` hashes both into provenance.json. LF checkout
# keeps their verified raw bytes identical across platforms.
crates/spoke-connect/bindings/cpp/include/spoke_connect.h text eol=lf
crates/spoke-connect/bindings/cpp/include/spoke_connect.hpp text eol=lf
